// Shared Syncthing ignore list for BOTH folders: `projects` (Mac mini
// ~/Documents/work/projects <-> MacBook Air ~/Projects, and mini -> NAS /data/projects)
// and `documents` (Mac mini ~/Documents -> NAS /data/documents).
//
// Goes at <folder root>/.stignore-shared on EVERY member of each folder. Each
// member's own .stignore is then a single line:
//
//     #include .stignore-shared
//
// .stignore is not itself synced by Syncthing; this file is. That indirection
// is the only reason the nodes cannot quietly drift apart on what they ignore
// -- editing it on one Mac updates every member.

// THE NESTING GUARD. `projects` lives INSIDE `documents` on the Mac mini
// (~/Documents/work/projects). Without this line the mini indexes that subtree
// twice, once per folder, and every MacBook change is re-announced through
// `documents` as a second, competing version. Anchored at the folder root, so
// it only ever matches in `documents`; in `projects` there is no `work/`.
/work/projects

// macOS metadata. Finder and Spotlight recreate these on demand; syncing them
// only produces churn, and on the NAS (POSIX, uid 568) they mean nothing.
// (?d) lets Syncthing delete them when it removes their directory.
(?d).DS_Store
(?d)._*
(?d).Spotlight-V100
(?d).Trashes
(?d).fseventsd
(?d).TemporaryItems
(?d).DocumentRevisions-V100
(?d).com.apple.timemachine.donotpresent

// .git IS DELIBERATELY NOT IGNORED. Ignoring it would leave the peers sharing
// a working tree with no branch, no history, and no way to restore a repo from
// this node -- the NAS copy would be a file dump rather than a backup. The
// cost is the rule in the README: do not have the same repo open and being
// written on both Macs at once.

// Build output and dependency trees. Large, high-churn, and reproducible from
// the manifests that ARE synced, so syncing them buys nothing and costs the
// small-file throughput this folder is already bound by.
(?d)node_modules
(?d).venv
(?d)venv
(?d)__pycache__
(?d)*.pyc
(?d)target
(?d)dist
(?d)build
(?d).direnv
(?d).tox
(?d).pytest_cache
(?d).mypy_cache
(?d).ruff_cache

// Helm vendored subcharts. This repo gitignores components/**/charts/ and
// re-fetches them with `helm dependency update`; syncing them would propagate
// a stale subchart from one machine to another, which is the exact failure the
// Rook version-coherence rule exists to prevent.
(?d)charts
